  "notes": "バズる is a slang verb meaning to go viral online. Derived from English \"buzz.\"\n\nCONJUGATION (godan verb):\n- バズる: dictionary form\n- バズった: past tense\n- バズらない: negative\n- バズって: te-form\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- SNSでバズる: to go viral on social media\n- バズった{動画|どうが}: a viral video\n- バズらせる: to make something go viral (causative)\n- バズり{狙|ねら}い: aiming to go viral\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- バズ: buzz, viral sensation (noun)\n- {炎上|えんじょう}: going viral for negative reasons (online controversy)\n- {拡散|かくさん}: spreading (of information)\n\nREGISTER:\nInternet slang. Very common among younger speakers and in social media contexts.",
